    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0814" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.5231/167: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-28T15:00:00+00:00">December 28, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 28—12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Recent exchange agreement with France<anchor n="38" xml:id="d605-f1"/>
                    summarized Commercial Attaché’s financial report week ended December 21st<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d605-f2"/> will obviously result in further increasing dollar
                    remittances delay. Moreover confidential official information just obtained that
                    Spain has offered England clearing agreement. Saw Sub-Secretary this morning who
                    states exchange situation is covered in pending commercial agreement of which we
                    still have no copy and adds that Spain is studying every means including that of
                    loan to normalize exchange with all countries.</p>
                <p>In view of the above developments believe early successful conclusion our
                    agreement more desirable than ever.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
